@startuml
title SHAKE128(M, d) end-to-end
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
}

start
:Message M, requested output length d;
:Append the 4-bit domain suffix 1111\n(distinguishes SHAKE from SHA-3 and cSHAKE);
:Apply pad10*1 to reach a multiple of\nthe rate, 1344 bits = 168 bytes\n(always adds at least 2 bits);
note right
  Byte form for a byte-aligned M:
  q = 1   -> 0x9F
  q = 2   -> 0x1F 0x80
  q > 2   -> 0x1F, zeros, 0x80
end note
:Initialise the state S to 1600 zero bits;
while (blocks left to absorb?) is (yes)
  :XOR the next 168-byte block into\nthe rate portion of S;
  :S = KECCAK-p[1600, 24](S);
endwhile (no)
:Z = empty;
:Append the first 168 bytes of S to Z;
while (len(Z) < d ?) is (yes)
  :S = KECCAK-p[1600, 24](S);
  :Append the next 168 bytes of S to Z;
endwhile (no)
:Return the first d bits of Z;
stop

note right
  d selects how many bits are returned,
  never which bits they are. This is why
  a shorter output is a prefix of a longer one.
end note
@enduml
